## Getting started

Requirements: Flutter {{flutter_version}}{{fvm_note}}, Xcode (iOS), Android SDK.

```sh
{{flutter}} pub get
{{flutter}} gen-l10n
```

## Flavors

The app has three flavors. Each has its own entry point, bundle id and app name, so all three can be installed side by side.

| Flavor | Entry point | Android applicationId / iOS bundle id | App name |
|---|---|---|---|
| development | `lib/main_development.dart` | `{{bundle_id}}.dev` | [DEV] {{app_name}} |
| staging | `lib/main_staging.dart` | `{{bundle_id}}.stg` | [STG] {{app_name}} |
| production | `lib/main_production.dart` | `{{bundle_id}}` | {{app_name}} |

```sh
# Run
{{flutter}} run --flavor development -t lib/main_development.dart
{{flutter}} run --flavor staging     -t lib/main_staging.dart
{{flutter}} run --flavor production  -t lib/main_production.dart

# Build
{{flutter}} build apk --flavor production -t lib/main_production.dart
{{flutter}} build ipa --flavor production -t lib/main_production.dart
```

VS Code users can pick a flavor from the Run and Debug panel (`.vscode/launch.json`).

Per-flavor settings such as the API base URL live in the `AppConfig` passed by each `main_<flavor>.dart`. Secrets are not committed. Pass them with `--dart-define` or `--dart-define-from-file` and read them with `String.fromEnvironment`.

## Project structure

```
lib/
├── main_<flavor>.dart   # picks the AppConfig, calls bootstrap()
├── bootstrap.dart       # DI, crash reporting, error hooks, Bloc observer, runApp
├── app/                 # root App widget (MaterialApp.router, theme, l10n)
├── di/                  # GetIt service locator + one module per area
├── core/                # contracts only: config, network, navigation, logger,
│                        #   crash, storage, image_resolver, domain/failures
├── shared/              # implementations of core contracts + theme, widgets
├── l10n/                # ARB files (arb/) and generated code (gen/)
└── features/<name>/     # data/ · domain/ · presentation/
```

Rules:
- Features depend on `core/` contracts, never on `shared/` implementations or on other features.
- Repositories return `Either<Failure, T>`.
- State is managed with Cubits.
- Navigate with typed routes: `context.nav.push(OrderDetailsRoute(orderId: id))`. Route classes live in `lib/shared/navigation/routes/`. Every `GoRoute` in `AppRouter` goes through `buildTypedPage`, which parses URL arguments and shows `InvalidRouteScreen` for broken links.
- Read colours and text styles with `context.colors` and `context.textTheme`, and spacing with `AppDimensions`.
- Show images with `ImageResourceResolver.<name>.getImageWidget()`.
- Get strings from `context.l10n`.

## State management

This project uses [flutter_bloc](https://bloclibrary.dev) Cubits. Each cubit lives in `features/<f>/presentation/cubits/` with a sealed `<X>State` in a `part` file. `AppBlocObserver` logs every transition in debug builds.

## Localization

Strings live in `lib/l10n/arb/app_en.arb`. To add a string:

1. Add the key and an `@key` description to `app_en.arb`.
2. Run `{{flutter}} gen-l10n`. This also runs automatically on `flutter run` and `flutter build`.
3. Use it as `context.l10n.yourKey`.

To add a language, create `app_<locale>.arb` with the same keys and add the locale to `CFBundleLocalizations` in `ios/Runner/Info.plist`.

## Testing

```sh
{{flutter}} test                 # all tests
{{flutter}} test --coverage      # with coverage → coverage/lcov.info
```

`test/` mirrors `lib/`. Widget tests use `tester.pumpApp(...)` from `test/helpers/pump_app.dart`, which provides the theme, localizations and a mock navigator. Shared mocks of the core contracts are in `test/helpers/mocks.dart`.

## Local CI

Run this before pushing:

```sh
scripts/local_ci.sh              # format, analyze, test + coverage gate, Android & iOS builds
scripts/local_ci.sh --skip-build # fast: checks and tests only
```

The coverage minimum defaults to 80%. Override it with `MIN_COVERAGE=90`.
